VDR Plugin 'zapcache' Revision History
--------------------------------------

2026-10-31: Version 0.2.0

- Service interface: the header can be included by C code, too. An output
  plugin gets the interface in cPlugin::Start(), before VDR switches to the
  first live channel.
- Service interface: the output device reports the first picture and the
  playback start of a channel switch (ReportSwitchEvent()), the zap cache
  measures the times. Every dropped or repeated frame is reported
  (ReportFrameCorrection()), the zap cache counts them within 5s after the
  playback start. Splice() returns the delay of the playback to the live
  stream (-1: not started with the buffer), SwitchCached() is gone.
- Radio channels are buffered: a switch to them starts with as much buffered
  audio, as the output device needs to start the playback.
- SVDRP commands STAT (status and statistics), RSTS (reset the statistics) and
  ENAB (switch the zap cache on or off).
- Service ZapCache-Channels-v1.0: any plugin can query the channels, which are
  received ahead.

2026-10-31: Version 0.1.0

- Initial version. The zap cache was part of the output plugin drmdevice
  (version 2.2.0) and is a plugin of its own now, so other output plugins can
  use it through the service interface (zapcache_service.h).
- The setup values are named zapcache.* (formerly drmdevice.ZapAhead*):
  Enable, Tuners, Release, SyncAudio, MaxDelay, Cam. The zap cache is on by
  default, when the plugin is loaded.
